# Every env file is ignored, including the VERCEL_OIDC_TOKEN that `vercel link`
# writes into .env.local.
.env*

# ...except the template, which must stay tracked.
#
# This negation has to come AFTER `.env*`: gitignore applies the LAST matching
# pattern, so a broad rule added below would silently re-ignore the example.
# `vercel link` appended exactly such a rule at the end of this file, and the
# only thing still protecting the template was that it was already tracked —
# `git check-ignore --no-index .env.example` showed the latent bug.
#
# It also overrides the broad `.env.*` in the global excludes file
# (~/.config/git/ignore), which is a good default that happens to catch
# templates too.
!.env.example

*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

.DS_Store
*.log
npm-debug.log*

coverage/
.vercel/
.vitest/

# Generated from wrangler.jsonc + the installed wrangler version by
